---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Climate & Agriculture | Food Supply Crisis Report"
  description="Understand how El Niño, drought, heat, rainfall and water stress can affect crops, food supply and food prices."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Topic hub</p>
      <h1>Climate &amp; Agriculture</h1>
      <p>Weather and climate risks can affect harvests, irrigation, livestock, food prices and agricultural resilience. The effect is usually regional and depends on the crop, season, water availability and starting conditions.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Follow the main climate drivers</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h2><a href="/articles/very-strong-el-nino-2026-food-production/">El Niño and crop risk</a></h2>
          <p>See how a very strong El Niño scenario could alter rainfall and crop conditions across exposed regions without implying a single global harvest outcome.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2><a href="/articles/germany-harvest-drought-food-prices-2026/">Drought and harvests</a></h2>
          <p>Examine how drought can reduce crop output and how a harvest shock can feed through to prices without guaranteeing a bread shortage.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2><a href="/articles/water-crisis-food-crisis/">Water stress and food production</a></h2>
          <p>Understand why irrigation, groundwater and long-term water availability matter for food production as well as short-term weather shocks.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>How to read climate-risk coverage</strong>
        <p>Climate conditions are one part of a wider food system. Trade routes, fertilizer, energy, inventories, policy and household purchasing power can amplify or offset a production shock.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
